  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Sunday)\nIssued at 245 AM CDT Mon Oct 5 2026\n\nWarm, above-normal temperatures and generally dry conditions will\ncontinue through next weekend. There remains high confidence that\nno significant cool down will occur, as indicated by minimal \nspread in bias-corrected probabilistic guidance through Sunday. \nHighs are forecast to remain in the 80s to low 90s deg F. There \nis only a low chance (15%) of showers/storms Friday across parts \nof western north Texas in association with an upper-level low in \nTexas. \n\nThere are some signs of a potential pattern change by early next \nweek (October 13-15) among deterministic models and some ensemble \nmembers, which could drive a cold front southward into the \nPlains. As a result, the temperature spread increases markedly \n(~30 deg F) in probabilistic guidance with the potential for an \nappreciable cold front passage. Currently, there is a 20% (south) \nto 50% (north) chance of high temperatures below 75 deg F on \nTuesday, October 13.\n\nMahale",
